// Probe 90 — Cluster IV-Spacial parser-hang isolation: self-referential
//             struct field
//
// If `Point` itself contains a `spacial<Point[...]>` field — a self-
// referential type — the parser may loop trying to recursively resolve
// `Point`'s layout (Point references spacial<Point>, which references
// Point, which references spacial<Point>, ...).
//
// If 90 PARSER-HANGS even at the type-declaration level: self-reference
// in keyed-collection types isn't terminated by a depth-cap.  Likely
// the same root cause as probe 51/62 — `Point[name]` makes the parser
// resolve `Point.name` (text), then `Point`'s OTHER fields (one of which
// might transitively reference Point again through some lookup).
//
// If 90 PARSES: self-reference isn't required for the hang; the
// minimal hang shape is probe 51/62 itself.
//
// Diagnostic invocation:
//   LOFT_TIMEOUT=8 LOFT_TIMEOUT_CLEAN_EXIT=1 ./target/release/loft \
//     --interpret 90-spacial-self-ref.loft
//
// Pairing: 51, 62, 88, 89.
// Status: cluster IV-Spacial isolation probe.

struct Node {
  name: text,
  x: float,
  y: float,
  // children: spacial<Node[name]>,   // ← uncomment if probe 89 hangs
                                       //   to test self-reference dimension
}

fn main() {
  n = Node { name: "root", x: 0.0, y: 0.0 };
  println("probe 90 PASSED (Node declared without spacial self-ref)");
}
